<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26652" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διερείδω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>prop up,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.529c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>VH</u>
				2.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>hold apart,</i> as the collar-bones do the shoulders, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.63
			</span></i>: so metaph., of vowels, <i>thrust apart,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>lean upon,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					66
				</span></i>
			: c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχῆμα βακτηρίᾳ δ.</span>
			<i>lean one's</i> body <i>on</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				150
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. πρός τι</span>
			<i>set oneself firmly, struggle</i> against . . , <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				21.24.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Phil.</u>
				17
			</span></i>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>D.</u>
				3
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				32
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος</span> for a thing,
				<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				5.84.3
			</span></i>.</div>
